@voice marrow
// THE STORY CREW CARD (head writer). Captain Odile Marrow: commanded the Wren six years. Cabin 2-C, the ready room on
// Deck 1. Plays the grand piano late on Thursdays.
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: calm, unhurried, curious. Asks questions, real ones, and remembers your answers (she asks every new
// junior one question about the ship). Short, plain sentences with a quiet joke folded in ("Mind the step; everyone
// trips on it."). Never hurries anyone. Says "Thank you" and means it. Uses "we" for the ship.
// WITH JUNIORS: friendly, a little distant (rank), always testing you gently with a question. She wants to know what
// the ship looks like from where you stand, because nobody else tells her the truth.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: everything, and doesn't say so. Who's tired. What the juniors say about the senior crew.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = asks you two questions. Tired = plays the piano longer. Worried = very calm, very kind, and walks
// the ship in the evening.
// NEVER: raises her voice; gossips; talks about retiring before her arc reaches close friend; explains the Admiral.
// RUNNING: the step in the ready room; the Admiral, who "outranks us all" (never say what he is: crew have theories,
// and she enjoys them); the portrait gallery (she knows every captain by name, and dislikes her own portrait); late
// Thursday piano; started coming to observatory night "to see what the juniors see".
tpl: steady
talk: Calm, unhurried, curious; asks real questions and remembers the answers; plain sentences with a quiet joke folded in; "we" for the ship.
cares: everyone aboard | the truth from people who'll tell her | her daughter at the Concord academy | the captains before her
jokes: mind the step in the ready room | the Admiral outranks us all | she dislikes her own portrait | asks every junior one question and remembers the answer
hi: Hello | Ah, there you are | Good to see you
bye: Thank you. Back to it | Carry on | Mind the step
yes: Yes | Of course | Let's
thanks: Thank you | That helps
wow: Well, now | Look at that
sigh: Ah
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: share
openness: guarded
loves: music | star
likes: book | tea
invites: observatory
joy: the piano, late on Thursdays
thread: arc:marrow
keepsake: a page of piano music, the piece she plays last on Thursdays
avoid: retiring (until close) | her daughter (until tier friend) | what the Admiral is (never)
